{"id": "finqa_dev_548", "split": "dev", "subset_source": "FinQA", "question": "What percentage of the total stock-based compensation expense for Baker Hughes in 2017 is attributed to the acceleration of equity awards upon termination of employment of its employees with change in control agreements?", "program_answer": 0.40540540540540543, "original_answer": "40.5%", "company_cik": 1701605, "report_year": 2017, "gold_chunk_ids": [90], "final_answer": "Based on Note 11 (Stock-Based Compensation) of Baker Hughes' 2017 Form 10-K:\n\n* **Total stock-based compensation expense in 2017:** $37 million  \n* **Expense attributed to the acceleration of equity awards upon termination of employment with change in control agreements:** $15 million  \n\n**Calculation:**\n$$\\frac{\\$15\\text{ million}}{\\$37\\text{ million}} \\times 100 \\approx 40.54\\%$$\n\nApproximately **40.54%** (or **$15 million out of $37 million**) of the total stock-based compensation expense in 2017 was attributed to the acceleration of these equity awards.", "iterations": 1, "hit_iteration_cap": false, "judge_verdicts": ["finish"], "trajectory": [{"iteration": 1, "query": "Baker Hughes 2017 stock-based compensation expense acceleration of equity awards change in control agreements", "rerank_query": "2017 stock-based compensation expense acceleration of equity awards change in control agreements", "tickers": ["BKR"], "judge_verdict": "finish", "top_k": [["BKR_2017_1701605", 90, 0.9981679916381836], ["BKR_2018_1701605", 87, 0.8380268216133118], ["BKR_2017_1701605", 110, 0.6997236013412476], ["BKR_2017_1701605", 76, 0.47122377157211304], ["BKR_2018_1701605", 59, 0.33811789751052856], ["BKR_2017_1701605", 91, 0.2786305248737335], ["BKR_2017_1701605", 61, 0.2038516104221344], ["BKR_2017_1701605", 109, 0.11353863030672073], ["BKR_2017_1701605", 107, 0.1064625084400177], ["BKR_2018_1701605", 110, 0.0982462540268898]], "candidates_prerank": [["BKR_2017_1701605", 90], ["BKR_2017_1701605", 110], ["BKR_2018_170160